{"id": "AR1-1", "type": "short", "tier": 2, "lang": "en", "category": "Operators", "subcat": "arithmetic", "question": "What does console.log print?", "code": "console.log(2 + 3 * 4);", "answer": "14", "hint": "Multiplication has higher precedence than addition.", "explain": "`3 * 4` evaluates first (12); then `2 + 12` → 14."}
{"id": "AR1-2", "type": "short", "tier": 2, "lang": "en", "category": "Operators", "subcat": "arithmetic", "question": "What does console.log print?", "code": "console.log((2 + 3) * 4);", "answer": "20", "hint": "Parentheses alter the default precedence.", "explain": "`(2 + 3)` is 5; `5 * 4` → 20."}
{"id": "AR1-3", "type": "short", "tier": 2, "lang": "en", "category": "Operators", "subcat": "arithmetic", "question": "What does console.log print?", "code": "console.log(10 / 4);", "answer": "2.5", "hint": "Integer division still produces a floating‑point number.", "explain": "JavaScript uses IEEE‑754 floating point; `10 / 4` is `2.5`."}
{"id": "AR1-4", "type": "short", "tier": 2, "lang": "en", "category": "Operators", "subcat": "arithmetic", "question": "What does console.log print?", "code": "console.log(10 % 4);", "answer": "2", "hint": "Remainder after division.", "explain": "`10 = 4*2 + 2`, so `10 % 4` is `2`."}
{"id": "AR1-5", "type": "short", "tier": 2, "lang": "en", "category": "Operators", "subcat": "arithmetic", "question": "What does console.log print?", "code": "console.log(2 ** 3 ** 2);", "answer": "512", "hint": "Exponentiation is right‑associative.", "explain": "Evaluates as `2 ** (3 ** 2)` → `2 ** 9` → 512."}
{"id": "AR1-6", "type": "short", "tier": 2, "lang": "en", "category": "Operators", "subcat": "arithmetic", "question": "What does console.log print?", "code": "console.log(-(3 ** 2));", "answer": "-9", "hint": "Unary minus applies after exponentiation here due to parentheses.", "explain": "`3 ** 2` is 9; unary minus yields `-9`."}
{"id": "AR1-7", "type": "short", "tier": 2, "lang": "en", "category": "Operators", "subcat": "arithmetic", "question": "What does console.log print?", "code": "console.log(5 + 4 / 2 - 3);", "answer": "4", "hint": "Do `4 / 2` before addition/subtraction.", "explain": "`4 / 2` → 2, then `5 + 2 - 3` → 4."}
{"id": "AR1-8", "type": "short", "tier": 2, "lang": "en", "category": "Operators", "subcat": "arithmetic", "question": "What does console.log print?", "code": "console.log(8 / (2 * (2 + 0)));", "answer": "2", "hint": "Work from the innermost parentheses.", "explain": "`(2 + 0)` → 2; `2 * 2` → 4; `8 / 4` → 2."}
